        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T19:11:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t remember if I noticed this code path before... With PV MMU we don\u0027t have any MMIO SPTEs, or any SPTEs in KVM-high at all. But I need to take a look if this is harmless or not.",
      "parentUuid": "5c092c45_a8d9ab2c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7285,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 7285,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "fec8f4f490e5784f9ad6784fbdeb4fcc8545aa86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a644475_0f565135",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/mmu/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 7285,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T09:53:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so, with PV MMU we don\u0027t have any MMIO SPTEs so we don\u0027t have to invalidate them. So we may just needlessly call kvm_mmu_zap_all_fast(), and that _might_ be a problem, at least because it triggers __kvm_mmu_free_obsolete_roots() which calls is_obsolete_root() assuming that mmu-\u003eroot.hpa is an address of an actual MMU root we\u0027ve allocated, which is not the case with PV MMU.\n\nSo it\u0027s better to explicitly disable kvm_mmu_invalidate_mmio_sptes() if enable_pkvm is true. In fact it seems we can disable it whenever enable_mmio_caching is false, not just with pKVM.\n\n...This also makes me think that it\u0027s probably better (at least cleaner) to explicitly prevent kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all() from calling kvm_mmu_zap_all() if enable_pkvm is true.",
      "parentUuid": "a0d922b4_b053793c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7285,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 7285,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "fec8f4f490e5784f9ad6784fbdeb4fcc8545aa86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73122ca0_1fa1c623",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/mmu/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 7285,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-06T13:32:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So it\u0027s better to explicitly disable kvm_mmu_invalidate_mmio_sptes() if enable_pkvm is true. In fact it seems we can disable it whenever enable_mmio_caching is false, not just with pKVM.\n\nDone in aosp/3790431 (https://lore.kernel.org/kvm/20250926135139.1597781-1-dmaluka@chromium.org/)\n\n\u003e This also makes me think that it\u0027s probably better (at least cleaner) to explicitly prevent kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all() from calling kvm_mmu_zap_all() if enable_pkvm is true.\n\nDone in aosp/3790430",
      "parentUuid": "2a644475_0f565135",
